{
  "description": "The large audio mesh of the scale run (owner, 22 November 2026: \"test on a larger deployed mesh\", \"with simulated users too\", audio only), merged topology: in each region two forwarders and 10 edges in sydney, 10 edges in london, 10 edges in newyork, 10 edges in tokyo, all g6-dedicated-2; listener load hosts 16 x g6-dedicated-4 in sydney, 8 x g6-dedicated-8 in london, 8 x g6-dedicated-8 in newyork, 8 x g6-dedicated-8 in tokyo (needletail-load for the UDP listeners, ntcmp for the LL-HLS ones) and a g6-dedicated-4 view host for the full probes, on the region's VLAN (Linode does not bill VLAN traffic; 5,000 UDP listeners of 1 ms PCM over the public network would be about 12 TB an hour of billed transfer), and a self-hosted LiveKit SFU (g6-dedicated-2) per region; the contributor alone on a g6-dedicated-4 in London with its source host lon-src. Dedicated plans only. Sydney first: the region short of capacity is created first; the run works without it (lab up --optional-sites sydney, or --without-sites sydney). Standby edges (syd-edge-6, syd-edge-7, syd-edge-8, syd-edge-9, syd-edge-10, lon-edge-6, lon-edge-7, lon-edge-8, lon-edge-9, lon-edge-10, new-edge-6, new-edge-7, new-edge-8, new-edge-9, new-edge-10, tok-edge-6, tok-edge-7, tok-edge-8, tok-edge-9, tok-edge-10): created, held out of the first curve by the deploy setting standby_edges, restarted in for the second. Sized for the owner's budget of 22 November (about $60 to $70 with the watchdog's cap): the referee's plan (needletail-compare target/compare/scale-plan.md) grown to as many listener hosts as it buys, and enough edges a region that on the second curve the edges give out before the listener hosts; Sydney's listener hosts are g6-dedicated-4, for it had no g6-dedicated-8 capacity on 22 November (same vCPUs, same price). Generated by scripts/scale_topology.py; the plan, the cost and the steps are in deploy/low-latency/SCALE.md.",
